      "writtenOn": "2018-08-08T09:19:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The previous implementation assumed that the destIp for a Nak should always be mClientIp (in some cases it should be the relay address), and that srcIp should be yiaddr (which is wrong and should be set all 0s for a NAK, we are not offering an address).\nIt also gave a false impression that the addresses were filled with actual values, even though those are never initialized. I thought explicitly using empty values makes it more clear, especially considering that we don\u0027t have a valid srcIp to fill in here.\n\nNote that this code is unused at the moment since DhcpClient does not build NAK packets.",
